<article class="env-lemma" id="D1C141">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D1C141">Lemma <span data-tag="D1C141">7.3.2.1</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos and $\emptyset $ an initial object of $\calX $. Then $\emptyset $ is $(-1)$-truncated. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X$ be an object of $\calX $. The space $\bHom _{\calX }(X, \emptyset )$ is contractible if $X$ is an initial object of $\calX $, and empty otherwise (by Lemma <a href="/tag/0FD9C4" data-tag="0FD9C4">6.1.3.6</a>). In either case, $\bHom _{\calX }(X, \emptyset )$ is $(-1)$-truncated. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>